---
number: 37
title: The Sun Is on the Land
author: Louis F. Benson
composer: Frederick C. Maker
sp_category: "3"
topic: Morning Worship
---

[verse 1]
The sun is on the land and sea,
The day begun;
Our morning hymn begins with Thee,
Most Holy One.
Our praise shall rise continually
Till day is done.

[verse 2]
Thy love was ever in our view,
Like stars by night;
Thy gifts are every morning new,
O God of light;
Thy mercy, like the heavens’ blue,
Fills all our sight.

[verse 3]
We do not know what grief or care
The day may bring;
The heart shall find some gladness there
That loves its King;
The life that serves Thee everywhere
Can always sing.

[verse 4]
All glory to the Father be,
With Christ the Son,
And, Holy Spirit, unto Thee,
Forever One;
All glory to the Holy Three,
While ages run.
